'''Ancient Egg: N201''' is a [[:Category:Special Cats|Special Cat]] that can be obtained from the [[June Bride of the Devil (Event Gacha)|June Bride of the Devil]] event. It was added in [[Version 11.6 Update|Version 11.6]]. [[True Form]] massively improves almost all attributes and grants Behemoth Slayer.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 665
|rarity = EX
|name1 = Ancient Egg: N201
|name2 = Dark Egg: N201
|name3 = Exorcist Cat
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Dark Egg: N201''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''Exorcist Cat''' at level 30 using [[Catfruit#Behemoth Stones|Behemoth Stones]] and XP.

==Strategy/Usage==
==='''Normal/Evolved Form'''===
These forms are <u>useless by design</u>. Similarly to the other [[:Category:Ancient Eggs|Ancient Eggs]], this unit is not meant to be used before its True Form. However, due to its somewhat low cost and quick recharge, it may be used as an emergency meatshield in [[Underground Labyrinth]] or [[Legend Quest]] if you have no use for its True Form.

==='''True Form'''===
Simply put, Exorcist Cat is a sub-par [[:Category:Anti-Aku Cats|anti-Aku]]. This boils down to a few problems, chief of which is the lack of [[Shield Piercing]]. Most Aku enemies have [[Shield]]s which block status effects. As such, while Exorcist is quite effective against them, something must get past the shield first. Exorcist Cat has no immunity to [[Surge Attack|Surges]], and many Aku possess the ability to release a Surge when attacking or dying. This is a huge problem for Exorcist Cat, as it doesn't have the health to survive even a weak Surge Attack. Lastly, Exorcist Cat has a disappointingly small range, further limiting his already-niche usage. Even its Behemoth Slayer is of little to no use, as all Aku Behemoths attack from range and deal way too much damage for it to handle. Considering the above points, Exorcist only really sees use against strong but isolated Aku threats, such as [[Infernal Tyrant Nyandam]].

